<WRAP important 100%>**Warning!!** 

The manufacturer had been using in 2023 a flash chip, Zbit Semiconductor part #ZB25VQ128ASIG. 

This isn't currently supported by OpenWRT, there's however an error report open at https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/issues/12306 

OpenWRT images supporting the new chip can be found at https://github.com/ThranduilII/openwrt/files/11399622/Openwrt-22.03.5-X5000R-Zbit-support.zip.

Until the issue's resolved, you CANNOT use any official OpenWRT image, only the one from the link above.

Please check your flash chip before flashing OpenWRT.

You will see the following message on the console if you have an unsupported chip

<code>
[    4.325094] spi-nor spi0.0: unrecognized JEDEC id bytes: 5e 40 18 5e 40 18
[    4.331987] spi-nor: probe of spi0.0 failed with error -2
</code>
An image of the chip can be found at https://forum.openwrt.org/t/got-stuck-on-system-running-in-recovery-initramfs-mode-totolink-x5000r/160442/115

Edit September 2023: There is even another Flash chip, which works with the regular OpenWRT builds. The part is labeled "XMC PPF39300_08" (or similar, hard to read)
Edit August 2024: Devices shipped with chip labled "qh128a 104hip eon" (EN25QH128A-104HIP), fully supported by OpenWRT. 
</WRAP>
