===== Back to stock firmware =====

[[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/howto-revert-totolink-x5000r-to-factory-firmware/110595?u=tmomas|Source]]

  - Poweroff / unplug power adapter from the router
  - Download the X5000R factory image from [[https://www.totolink.net/home/menu/detail/menu_listtpl/download/id/218/ids/36.html]]
  - Set your computer ethernet IP to 192.168.1.X, subnet 255.255.255.0 (X=your chosen ip number ranging from 2-254)
  - Press and hold reset button while turn on / plug power adapter to the router. Wait untill ALL LAN green LED turn on, then release the reset button.
  - Plug the LAN cable from your computer into LAN 1 port
  - Confirm that you can connect to the router by ping 192.168.1.1 from command prompt / terminal
  - If you get reply from 192.168.1.1, then open web browser, and type in the address column : 192.168.1.1
  - You will get the X5000R firmware update page, then choose the factory-firmware file from previously downloaded file
  - Wait untill the router finish flashing (the router will reboot by itself) : Blue led dan green LAN led will blinking
  - Revert the computer ethernet ip to automatic
  - Open in web browser : itotolink.net or 192.168.0.1
  - Finish, you should get Totolink web gui config page


